      "spam": false,
      "value": "I would love this, but as it stands the game is having trouble performing well on a lot of clients.\nDoes anyone know if it would cause more performance troubles? I’m pretty sure it would but I don’t have loads of experience with Unity.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2017-12-21T17:44:09.590Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A way to record the data of what happens in-game, and then save a video of it. \n\nExample: this recent moment between Nagzz and Matsix. Very fun and cool, but would be even better with such a system. So maybe during replay of a scene we recorded, we could go back and retroactively turn off nameplates, mute or remove people who are distracting from the scene, so we only get the audio/video we want. If you've seen this video, there's a LOT of background noise from lots of talking by everybody else. Would be helpful to remove some of the swarm of people and nameplates so a better video can be saved.\n\nHow would people be muted or removed? Same way we do now, except when in a replay, muting or blocking a person only applies to that recording, making them silent or disappear.",
